## COURSE INFORMATION

**Course Title:** It Takes a Village: Collaborative Care and Ethical Consultation

**Course Description:** The African proverb "It takes a village to raise a child" captures a fundamental truth about human flourishing—we cannot do it alone. The same principle applies to mental health treatment, where complex clients require collaborative care involving multiple providers, disciplines, and systems. This comprehensive 3-hour course examines the art and ethics of consultation, coordination, and collaboration in clinical practice. From seeking consultation for difficult cases to providing it to colleagues, from navigating referrals ethically to coordinating care across multi-disciplinary teams, participants will develop competencies essential for effective practice in today's integrated healthcare landscape.

**Target Audience:** Licensed Professional Counselors, Licensed Mental Health Counselors, National Certified Counselors, Licensed Clinical Social Workers, Licensed Marriage and Family Therapists, Psychologists, Psychiatric Nurse Practitioners, and graduate-level counseling students.

**Credit Hours:** 3.0 CE Hours (Ethics/Clinical Practice)

**Course Level:** Intermediate

**Delivery Method:** Asynchronous Online Learning

**Content Area:** Professional Ethics and Practice

