Upon successful completion of this course, participants will be able to:

1. Distinguish between consultation, supervision, and collaborative care models and apply each appropriately in clinical practice.

2. Implement ethical procedures for seeking and providing clinical consultation in accordance with ACA Code of Ethics and state licensing requirements.

3. Navigate the referral process effectively, including assessment of when to refer, identification of appropriate resources, and warm handoff techniques.

4. Coordinate care with other providers while maintaining appropriate confidentiality and professional boundaries.

