# POST-TEST ANSWER KEY

| Question | Correct Answer | Rationale |
|----------|---------------|-----------|
| 1 | C | Research shows 45%+ have multiple diagnoses; 60%+ in clinical settings |
| 2 | B | Problems interact in ways that amplify each other |
| 3 | B | Allostatic load is the cumulative burden of chronic stress |
| 4 | A | The Four Ps: Predisposing, Precipitating, Perpetuating, Protective |
| 5 | B | Problem interaction maps identify how problems maintain each other |
| 6 | C | DBT hierarchy: life-threatening > therapy-interfering > quality of life |
| 7 | C | Keystone problems have outsized influence on multiple other areas |
| 8 | B | Sleep disruption maintains multiple conditions and is highly modifiable |
| 9 | C | The Unified Protocol targets shared mechanisms across disorders |
| 10 | B | Targeting shared mechanisms addresses multiple conditions simultaneously |
| 11 | C | Every session checks for safety issues before proceeding |
| 12 | C | Collaborative care prevents fragmentation and gaps |
| 13 | B | Crisis time + deeper work honors immediate needs while enabling progress |
| 14 | B | Complex cases take a toll requiring intentional self-care |
| 15 | B | Nonlinear progress is normal, not treatment failure |
| 16 | B | Multiple conditions require multiple lenses and services |
| 17 | C | Sufficient assessment enables informed treatment; perfect assessment is impossible |
| 18 | B | Broad screening ensures important issues aren't missed |
| 19 | B | Integrative conceptualization identifies how pieces fit together |
| 20 | C | Skilled complex case management expands access for underserved clients |

